The Icon Program Library (IPL), as gcon ships it, copied from the
reference implementation, github.com/gtownsend/icon, by
tools/ipl/update.sh:

  procs, gprocs   the procedure libraries, which link finds
  incl, gincl     the include files, which $include finds
  gprogs, gpacks  the programs Arizona's ipl/BuildBin builds into its bin
                  (colrbook, colrpick, fontpick, palette, wevents,
                  xgamma; vib), which gcon's build.sh builds into the
                  root's bin
  cfuncs          the C functions, which build.sh builds into the
                  root's lib/libcfunc.so; procs/cfunc.icn, their Icon
                  interface, is made by cfuncs/mkfunc.sh

The rest of the IPL (its other programs, packages, data and documents)
is in Arizona Icon's repository. UPSTREAM records the commit and each
file's SHA-256.

A few files are changed for gcon, whose display server is icon-sdl's
SDL backend (gcon predefines _SDL_GRAPHICS, not _X_WINDOW_SYSTEM): the
changes are icon-sdl's, made by tools/ipl/patch.sh, marked "# gcon:" in
the files, and listed in UPSTREAM.

gcon searches procs and gprocs after IPATH (for link), and incl and
gincl after LPATH (for $include). To change a file, copy it to a
directory on IPATH or LPATH rather than editing it here, or add a
change to tools/ipl/patch.sh.

These files are in the public domain, as the reference implementation's
README says of its material: "You may use and copy this material freely.
This privilege extends to modifications, although any modified version of
this system given to a third party should clearly identify your
modifications as well as the original source."

The one exception is gprocs/cardbits.icn, whose playing-card bitmaps
carry copyright and permission notices from Sun Microsystems, Network
Computing Devices and their authors. As a precaution those notices are
reproduced in NOTICE at the top of the gcon tree, as they ask.
